        "506": { n: "Substrate cleaning", t: "STO NOSTROY 2.9.136-2013 cl.5.3.2.2. Substrate must be cleared of debris, dust, dirt, and ice" },
        "507": { n: "Adhesive mix, water temperature when mixing mortar", t: "STO NOSTROY 2.9.136-2013.\nGOST 31357; GOST 28013; Project\nWater temperature not less than +5° C.\nIn winter, use winter-grade adhesive only." },
        "508": { n: "Vertical and horizontal masonry joints", t: "STO NOSTROY 2.9.136-2013 Table 9.1, Work Method Statement\nDesign thickness of horizontal and vertical joints should be taken as 2 +/- 1 mm. Actual joint thickness in the structure must not exceed 3 mm" },
        "509": { n: "Flatness and dust removal of the bedding surface of each masonry course", t: "STO NOSTROY 2.9.136-2013 cl.6.1.2, Work Method Statement\nEach course must be checked for flatness of the bedding surface. Steps between adjacent blocks detected with a straightedge must be removed by sanding. The sanded surface must be dedusted." },
        "510": { n: "Thickness of the bottom levelling layer of the first course", t: "STO NOSTROY 2.9.136-2013 cl.6.1.4, Work Method Statement\nFor the first course, the thickness of the continuous levelling mortar joint may range from 6 to 30 mm depending on the substrate surface." },
        "511": { n: "Uniform application of adhesive mortar, joint filling without gaps", t: "SP 70.13330.2012; Work Method Statement\nGaps in the adhesive mortar application are not permitted" },
        "512": { n: "Correctness of joint bonding pattern", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 cl. 9.2.1, Work Method Statement\nOffset of vertical joints in the course pattern not less than 100 mm." },
        "513": { n: "Masonry reinforcement", t: "STO NOSTROY 2.9.136-2013 cl.5.1.8, 5.3.2.15, 5.3.3.3\nAs per the project. Every 3rd course + openings\n- reinforcement with single deformed bars should be placed in mortar-filled chases cut into the bedding surface of the reinforced course;\n- reinforcing meshes for thin joints made of corrosion-resistant or corrosion-protected steel, in the form of flat working-reinforcement bars up to 2 mm thick, joined by butt-welded round wire, may be used;\n- masonry may also be reinforced with single bars of strip corrosion-resistant or corrosion-protected perforated steel not thicker than 2 mm" },
        "514": { n: "Wall thickness control", t: "STO NOSTROY 2.9.136-2013 Table 9.1;\nWork Method Statement\nTolerance «- 5 ; +5 mm»" },
        "515": { n: "Filling of gaps between the last masonry course and vertical building elements", t: "Work Method Statement, per the project" },
        "516": { n: "Installation of lintels over openings as per the project and standards", t: "SP 70.13330.2012; Work Method Statement, Project\nFor an opening width up to 1 m — bearing left and right min. 100 mm. It is not recommended to have a vertical joint of partition blocks under the bearing part.\nFor an opening width up to 1.1 m — bearing left and right min. 100 mm, and along the entire length onto class AIII reinforcement anchored to the wall with a mandatory vertical mortar joint. The reinforcement is embedded into the RC wall to a recommended depth of 80 mm, with the other end of the bar run into the masonry not less than 250 mm,\nFor a width up to 1.6 m — clamp in the masonry as a cantilever with a bearing of not less than 400 mm (1/3), with bottom reinforcement by class A-III steel reinforcement, with the ends of the reinforcing bar run into the masonry structure not less than 250 mm." },
        "517": { n: "Weakening of masonry structures by grooves, chases, niches, openings", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 cl. 9.1.4; Work Method Statement" },
        "518": { n: "Number of anchors and correctness of installation (wall, ceiling)", t: "Project, WEP, Work Method Statement\nFastening spacing every 2-3 blocks.\nReinforcement diameter 6-8 mm.\nBar length not less than 250 mm." },
        "519": { n: "Deviation of wall planes and corners from vertical", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 Table 9.8; Work Method Statement\nTolerance not more than 10 mm over the full storey height" },
        "520": { n: "Irregularities on the vertical masonry surface detected with a 2 m straightedge", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 Table 9.8; Work Method Statement\nTolerance not more than 10 mm." },
        "521": { n: "Block laying free of soiling, mortar squeeze-out and hollows.", t: "SP 70.13330.2012; Work Method Statement" },
        "522": { n: "Deviation in pier width", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 Table 9.8; Work Method Statement\nTolerance from 0 to «-15 mm»" },
        "523": { n: "Deviation in opening width", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 Table 9.8; Work Method Statement\nTolerance from 0 to «+15 mm»" },
        "524": { n: "Offset from the design position of setting-out axes", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 Table 9.8; Work Method Statement\nTolerance – 10 mm" },
        "525": { n: "Offset of window-opening vertical axes from vertical", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 Table 9.8;\nTolerance – 20 mm" },
        "526": { n: "Elevation deviation of the underside of lintel bearing surfaces", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 Table 9.8; Work Method Statement\nTolerance «- 10 mm»" },
        "527": { n: "Deviation from horizontal of laid lintels", t: "SP 70.13330.2012; Work Method Statement\nTolerance - 10 mm" },

