        "4214": { n: "Deviation from vertical of the top of planes", t: "≤10 mm\nSP 70.13330.2012 Table 6.1" },
        "4215": { n: "Vertical masonry joints", t: "Work Method Statement\nVertical joining of whole blocks is done without mortar, by joining the groove and tongue of the blocks being laid, with the joints grouted on both sides with mortar mix. A vertical joint is made with mortar only when joining:\n two sawn blocks;\n one sawn and one whole block;  abutment to the building frame;" },
        "4216": { n: "Thickness of horizontal masonry joints", t: "Work Method Statement\nHorizontal joint thickness must be 10 (+/-2) mm" },
        "4217": { n: "Uniform filling of joints with mortar", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 cl. 9.2.5, 9.2.6; Work Method Statement\nIncluding at the abutment of edge blocks to the walls over the full depth" },
        "4218": { n: "Horizontality of masonry courses", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 Table 9.8; Work Method Statement, up to 15 mm per 10 m of wall length" },
        "4219": { n: "Correctness of joint bonding pattern", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 cl. 9.2.1; Work Method Statement. Not less than 90 mm and not more than 410 mm" },
        "4220": { n: "Wall thickness control", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 Table 9.8; Work Method Statement\nTolerance ±15 mm." },
        "4221": { n: "Filling of gaps between the last masonry course and vertical building elements", t: "SP 70.13330.2012; Work Method Statement" },
        "4222": { n: "Installation of lintels over openings", t: "SP 70.13330.2012; Work Method Statement\nFor an opening width up to 1 m - bearing to the right and left min. 100 mm. It is not recommended that a vertical joint of partition blocks be located under the bearing part.\nFor an opening width up to 1,1 m - bearing to the right and left min. 100 mm, and along the entire length on class AIII reinforcement to the wall with a mandatory vertical mortar joint. The reinforcement is anchored into the reinforced concrete wall to the recommended depth of 80 mm, with the other end of the bar embedded in the masonry by not less than 250 mm,\nFor a width up to 1,6 m - clamp in the masonry like a cantilever with bearing of not less than 400 mm. (1/3) with bottom reinforcement of class A-III metal rebar, with the end portions of the reinforcing bar embedded by not less than 250 mm into the masonry structure." },
        "4223": { n: "Masonry bonding", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 cl. 9.2.1; Work Method Statement\nBonding of masonry with a course offset of ½ of the unit length and not less than 1/3" },
        "4224": { n: "Deviation of wall planes and corners from vertical", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 (Table 9.8); Work Method Statement\nTolerance not more than 10 mm over the full storey height" },
        "4225": { n: "Irregularities on the vertical masonry surface.", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 (Table 9.8); Work Method Statement\nTolerance not more than 5 mm over the full storey height" },
        "4226": { n: "SKT block laying free of soiling, mortar squeeze-out and hollows.", t: "SP 70.13330.2012; Work Method Statement" },
        "4227": { n: "Deviation in pier width", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 (table 9.8); Work Method Statement Tolerance from 0 to « -15mm»" },
        "4228": { n: "Deviation in opening width", t: "SP 70.13330.2012 (Table 9.8); Work Method Statement\nTolerance from 0 to «+15 mm»" },
