        "4244": { n: "Reveal width", t: "\"SP 71.13330.2017\" Table 7.4.\nDeviation from design width not more than 2 mm" },
        "4245": { n: "K2\nSurfaces with ordinary requirements for decorative properties (surfaces intended for facing works with elements of area not less than 900 cm2, application of decorative plasters with grain size over 1 mm, for structural paints and coatings, for gluing heavy wallpaper", t: "\"SP 71.13330.2017\" cl. 7.3.7, Table 7.5 Scratches, pits, gouges with a depth of not more than 1 mm are permitted (continuous visual inspection). Shadows from side lighting are permitted" },
        "4246": { n: "K3\nSurfaces with increased requirements for decorative properties (surfaces intended for facing works with small-piece and transparent elements, application of decorative plasters with grain size under 1 mm, for non-structural matte paints and coatings, gluing paper-based and non-woven wallpaper)", t: "\"SP 71.13330.2017\" cl. 7.3.7, Table 7.5 Marks from the abrasive used for sanding the surface are permitted, but not deeper than 0,3 mm (continuous visual inspection).\nShadows from side lighting are permitted" },
        "4247": { n: "Installation of the edge/perimeter damping strip", t: "\"SP 71.13330.2017\". Per the project.\nMonolithic screeds must be isolated from walls and partitions by strips of waterproofing materials and damper tapes. Thickness ≥10 mm. No breaks" },
        "4248": { n: "Deviation from horizontal and local irregularities", t: "WEP. Slope up to 0.2 % but not more than 20 mm per room. When installing a waterproofing coating – 5 mm\nScreeds under laminate, parquet, linoleum – 2 mm\nLeveling screeds under other types of coverings – 4 mm" },
        "4249": { n: "Installation of thermal/shrinkage control joints", t: "Project, WEP, SP 29.13330.2011, cl. 8.14. Spacing ≤6 m. At boundaries between different rooms." },
        "4250": { n: "Quality of smoothing of the finished screed surface", t: "WEP. \"SP 71.13330.2017\" Table 8.2. No visible defects, surface roughness, well smoothed" },
        "4251": { n: "Compressive strength of the finished screed after 28 days", t: "SP 29.13330.2011, cl. 8.5, Work Method Statement ≥15 MPa" },
        "4252": { n: "Absence of visible defects", t: "Work Method Statement, WEP. Not permitted: cracks Width ≤0,5 mm, length ≤100 mm, corner curling." },
        "4253": { n: "Polymer mastic", t: "\"SP 71.13330.2017\" cl. 8.6.4, 8.6.5.\nGaps are not permitted. Application of at least 2 layers. At the junctions of the floor with the walls, the waterproofing must be continuous to a height of at least 200 mm from the floor covering level, and where water jets may hit the walls - over the entire height of wetting. Reinforce corners by pressing mesh into the layer according to the manufacturer's instructions and the project." },
        "4254": { n: "Cement-based mortars", t: "\"SP 71.13330.2017\" cl. 8.6.4, 8.6.5.\nGaps are not permitted. Application of at least 2 layers. At the junctions of the floor with the walls, the waterproofing must be continuous to a height of at least 200 mm from the floor covering level, and where water jets may hit the walls - over the entire height of wetting. Reinforce corners by pressing mesh into the layer according to the manufacturer's instructions and the project. Cement-based mortar waterproofing shall be reinforced with a metal mesh with cell sizes from 10 x 10 to 20 x 20 mm or with polymer material meshes, unless otherwise specified by the material manufacturer." },
